## Why This Is Asked
Tests the ability to craft a robust online ICA chain that gracefully handles dynamic sensor availability in a real-world, latency-constrained setting.

## Key Concepts
- Dynamic active-channel management (4–6)
- Forgetting-factor whitening for nonstationarity
- Strategy switching: per-bin ICA vs joint diagonalization
- Dropout imputation via subspace projection
- Cross-bin permutation maintenance under channel changes
- Low-latency real-time constraints and evaluation plan

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudocode: frame processing
function processFrame(frame) {
  const active = detectActiveMics(frame);
  const W = whitening(frame, forgettingFactor);
  const strategy = chooseStrategy(active, sparsity(frame));
  const demixed = demix(frame, W, strategy);
  alignPermutation(demixed);
  return demixed;
}
```

